Z||000004||theogre||10-03-2000||08:15 PM||||do a search on cavalier.... we've covered that. They aren't programable except for changing them to metric. (I forget how you do that.) Those dashes look kind of nice, problem is finding one that works. Every one I've seen has some type of problem with the driver circuit for the flouresent display. (It records data. you can't see it.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||10-04-2000||11:05 AM||||I have been spending a lot of time with digital dash research. Ogre is right about finding a good one. The only great thing about the Cavalier dash is it FITS perfectly into a Fiero instrument pod. <BR>It is pretty lackluster in features. The button for MPH/KM is right on the front. Also the cavaliers (and Caddy Cimmeron) had both 2.5 and 2.8 engines so no need to play with tach accuracy. I got a good working dash from a Pontiac 6000STE but it is about 20" wide and 4" tall. Just for playing with. The nicest digital dash I ever saw from GM was in an Oldsmobile Trofeo. The gas gauge was switchable from full scale to just showing the last 1/4 tank as full scale. Nice feature. Unfortunatly this dash has 3 CPU chips and gets data from the cars computer and is not independent. Lots of Chryslers had digital dashes and most of the early ones (80's) are pretty lame looking gauges. I am still looking for a working GM instrument pod at the junkyard. They only cost $11.00 each.<BR>so I already have 4 to play with. The liquid crystal ones from Berettas' and Grand-Ams' are not very interesting lit up. I like the florescent ones best.<BR>the 4 I have to play with are<BR>89 Beretta - LCD works<BR>89 Grand AM - LCD works <BR>88 600STE - Florescent 199999 miles! V6<BR>86 Cimmeron - DEAD<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||10-04-2000||11:24 AM||||1FST2M6, I don't think you will find anyone here with the FDD-X1 since I haven't sold it in the States yet. Currently it's undergoing a redesign to make the tachometer a bit more stable. As it is right now it will work flawlessly in most Fieros but in some it is very unstable. The cause is because some Fieros use non-standard tachfilters or other non-standard parts which cause the unstabilities. As soon as the redesign is done, we'll start selling it in the States.||||reg||1
